{"name":"Incident with Codespaces","status":"resolved","created_at":"2026-02-02T20:17:19.554Z","updated_at":"2026-02-03T20:45:16.231Z","monitoring_at":null,"resolved_at":"2026-02-03T00:54:54.466Z","impact":"major","shortlink":"https://stspg.io/flvngz4l79b5","scheduled_for":null,"scheduled_until":null,"scheduled_remind_prior":false,"scheduled_reminded_at":null,"impact_override":"major","scheduled_auto_in_progress":false,"scheduled_auto_completed":false,"metadata":{},"started_at":"2026-02-02T20:17:19.547Z","reminder_intervals":null,"id":"t4s6xgbwv60j","page_id":"kctbh9vrtdwd","incident_updates":[{"status":"resolved","body":"On February 2, 2026, GitHub Codespaces were unavailable between 18:55 and 22:20 UTC and degraded until the service fully recovered at February 3, 2026 00:15 UTC. During this time, Codespaces creation and resume operations failed in all regions. \u003cbr /\u003e\u003cbr /\u003eThis outage was caused by a backend storage access policy change in our underlying compute provider that blocked access to critical VM metadata, causing all VM create, delete, reimage, and other operations to fail. More information is available at https://azure.status.microsoft/en-us/status/history/?trackingId=FNJ8-VQZ. This was mitigated by rolling back the policy change, which started at 22:15 UTC.  As VMs came back online, our runners worked through the backlog of requests that hadn’t timed out. \u003cbr /\u003e\u003cbr /\u003eWe are working with our compute provider to improve our incident response and engagement time, improve early detection before they impact our customers, and ensure safe rollout should similar changes occur in the future. We recognize this was a significant outage to our users that rely on GitHub’s workloads and apologize for the impact this had.","created_at":"2026-02-03T00:54:54.466Z","wants_twitter_update":false,"twitter_updated_at":null,"updated_at":"2026-02-03T20:45:16.226Z","display_at":"2026-02-03T00:54:54.466Z","deliver_notifications":true,"twe